# GitHub Commit & Push Lock (4778)

**Default: LOCKED.** Do not run `git commit`, `git push`, or open pull requests unless the operator explicitly authorizes it in the **same message** using this exact pattern:

```
4778 i want to commit <short description> to github
```

## Required for any git write

| Action | Allowed without 4778 commit phrase? |
|--------|-------------------------------------|
| `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` | Yes (read-only) |
| `git add`, `git commit`, `git push` | **No** |
| `gh pr create`, force push, amend | **No** |

## Passcode + intent

- Passcode **`4778` alone is not enough** — the message must also state commit/push intent (e.g. "commit … to github" or "push … to github").
- Without that phrase: implement locally only; tell the operator changes are uncommitted and waiting for authorization.

## Examples

| Operator message | Action |
|------------------|--------|
| "fix the live page" | Code only — no commit/push |
| "push to github" | **Stop** — need 4778 + explicit commit phrase |
| "4778 i want to commit live countdown fix to github" | Proceed with commit and push if requested |

## Attendee zone

Attendee-side **code** edits still require passcode **4778** per `attendee-side-passcode-lock.mdc`. This rule is separate: it governs **git operations**, not file edit authorization.
